OL,3,GNEWSA'Why we flushed away Dragons' Den
OL,4,Ainvestment'
OL,5,
OL,6,FWalking out of the Dragons' Den with an
OL,7,Finvestment from Deborah Meaden might
OL,8,Fsound like the perfect ending for a
OL,9,Ffledgling business.
OL,11,FBut Amber Probyn, from Ross-on-Wye, and
OL,12,FHazel McShane, from Norfolk, ultimately
OL,13,Fdecided to flush their deal away.
OL,15,FThe founders of PEEQUAL, which makes
OL,16,Fwhat it describes as the UK's first
OL,17,Fwomen's urinals, accepted an offer from
OL,18,FMeaden after pitching their
OL,19,Frevolutionary product in Thursday
OL,20,Fnight's episode.
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
